@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.7.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.7.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.7.0 (2026-11-20): The single-source step is built and checked on a toy source. Story ST11_Make is Done; the generic check story is next."""@en .

ex:TK11_Make_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "08-tooling/code_source_make_v1_0_0.py reads one source file per chapter and writes the manifest, the examples module for the generic deck builder (setup lines kept apart and never shown) and the Slide code tab. The source is refused on a missing field, a repeated id, a prompt line, a lambda or an order that is not slide order. No chapter text in the tool." .
ex:TK11_Make_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Log 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0/make_toy_run.log: two runs give identical files; the tab runs; slide code equals manifest code equals tab lines for 3 of 3 examples; four deliberately broken copies (prompt, lambda, wrong order, repeated id) are each refused. Run by the agent that wrote the tool, so not independent. Limit named: proven on a toy source of three examples; the real chapter 10 source and the builder reading the setup lines come in the chapter 10 stories. On Linux a Path prints with / where the book shows WindowsPath; the chapter 10 code story decides how results are shown." .
ex:ST11_Make backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met on a toy source; see its tasks." .
